# Company Identity Standards

**CRITICAL:** The company has rebranded. All new code and documentation MUST use the correct names.

## Identity

| Entity | Correct Name | WRONG Names (never use) |
|--------|-------------|------------------------|
| **Company** | Fractional Forge | Centaur Dynamics, CentaurOS (as company) |
| **App / Operating System** | ForgeOS | CentaurOS, Centaur OS |
| **Platform users** | Forge teams | Centaur teams |

## Usage Examples

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<title>Product X-Ray | ForgeOS</title>
<p>Welcome to ForgeOS</p>
<p>Fractional Forge builds ForgeOS, the operating system for fractional teams.</p>
<meta name="description" content="ForgeOS - The Democratic Workflow Engine" />

// ❌ WRONG - Old branding
<title>Product X-Ray | CentaurOS</title>
<p>Welcome to CentaurOS</p>
<p>Centaur Dynamics builds CentaurOS...</p>
```

## Where to Apply

- **Page titles:** `Something | ForgeOS`
- **UI copy:** Reference "ForgeOS" for the app, "Fractional Forge" for the company
- **Meta tags / manifest:** Use "ForgeOS"
- **Documentation:** Use "ForgeOS" for the product, "Fractional Forge" for the company
- **Comments/JSDoc:** Use "ForgeOS"
- **Cursor rules/skills:** Use "ForgeOS"
- **Marketing copy:** "Fractional Forge" (company), "ForgeOS" (product)

## What NOT to Change

- **Git repository URLs** (they are what they are)
- **Already-applied database migration files** (historical records)
- **Foundry IDs in database** (`centaur-guild`, `centaur-suppliers` - these are internal IDs, not user-facing)
- **Font file names** (`centaur-font-*.woff2` - file renames require separate coordination)
- **Image file names** (require actual file renames + deployment)
- **Sentry project name** (requires Sentry dashboard change)
- **Docker container names** (requires infra coordination)

## Hashtags / Tags

- Project tag: `#ForgeOS` (was `#CentaurOS`)
- Memory logging: Use `#ForgeOS` in daily logs

## Quick Check

Before committing, grep for these patterns and fix any new occurrences:
```bash
rg -i "centauros" --type ts --type tsx -l
rg "Centaur Dynamics" --type ts --type tsx -l
```
